  "hints": [
    "Sort a copy of nums first so duplicates are adjacent and two pointers work cleanly.",
    "For each index i: skip if i > 0 and arr[i] == arr[i - 1]. Use lo = i + 1, hi = n - 1 and skip duplicate lo / hi values after recording a matching triplet.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  arr = sorted(nums)\n  for i in range(n - 2):\n      if i > 0 and arr[i] == arr[i-1]: continue\n      two-pointer sweep over (i+1, n-1)"
